From 3f31a87f825fba582ad4c0ae84029628cc5dbf60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:58:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native V2 index of blocks whose children precede
 their parents

Port the Rust fix: V2Db::Connect and the disconnect undo validation
resolve, spend and plan asset events in a parents-first order
(ProcessingOrder: in-block parents before their children, otherwise block
order), since the ABC host confirms blocks in canonical (txid) order. The
explorer input check accepts a creation anywhere else in the same block,
and asset planning accepts a first event at a later position in the same
block. Tests cover a canonical-order block with chained spends and an
in-block mint (connect, replay, disconnect, reconnect, equal asset counts
to the topological order) and the ordering itself.

Tier: V2
